| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2015|3|3}}
| Viewers         = 4.48<ref name="2.11">{{Cite web |last=Bibel |first=Sara |date=March 4, 2015 |title=Tuesday Final Ratings: 'Chicago Fire' Adjusted Down; No Adjustment to 'Marvel's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.' |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/03/04/tuesday-final-ratings-chicago-fire-adjusted-down-no-adjustment-to-marvels-agents-of-s-h-i-e-l-d/370744/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150509005245/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/03/04/tuesday-final-ratings-chicago-fire-adjusted-down-no-adjustment-to-marvels-agents-of-s-h-i-e-l-d/370744/ |archive-date=May 9, 2015 |access-date=March 4, 2015 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = In the wake of Triplett's death, Coulson looks to hit back at Hydra, who are considering having Bakshi fill Whitehall's leadership position. S.H.I.E.L.D. enacts a plan that sees Bakshi escape and lead them to other high-ranking Hydra agents, who are then killed. In San Juan, the alien city is flooded, but not before a transformed Raina escapes, now with a monstrous appearance. When Cal turns his back on her, reminding her that she got what she wanted, Raina attempts to commit suicide, but she is taken by the man with no eyes, [[Gordon (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Gordon]], who can teleport. Fitz and Skye realize that the latter has also been transformed—she caused the earthquake in San Juan, but has no control over this ability. Fitz agrees to keep her secret and hides the truth from the rest of the team. Meanwhile, a model car that Mack built for Coulson scans the latter's office and finds the "toolbox" that previous S.H.I.E.L.D. Director [[Nick Fury (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Nick Fury]] gave to him. Mack, who has been studying the S.H.I.E.L.D. base's schematics, secretly reports this to Morse.
| LineColor       = 881E1E
}}
