| EpisodeNumber   = 38
| EpisodeNumber2  = 16
| Title           = [[Afterlife (Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.)|Afterlife]]
| DirectedBy      = [[Kevin Hooks]]
| WrittenBy       = Craig Titley
| OriginalAirDate = {{Start date|2015|4|7}}
| Viewers         = 4.24<ref name="2.16">{{Cite web |last=Kondolojy |first=Amanda |date=April 8, 2015 |title=Tuesday Final Ratings: 'NCIS: New Orleans' Adjusted Up; No Adjustment for 'Forever', 'New Girl' or 'Weird Loners' |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/04/08/tuesday-final-ratings-ncis-new-orleans-adjusted-up-no-adjustment-for-forever-new-girl-or-weird-loners/386241/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150414190713/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/04/08/tuesday-final-ratings-ncis-new-orleans-adjusted-up-no-adjustment-for-forever-new-girl-or-weird-loners/386241/ |archive-date=April 14, 2015 |access-date=April 8, 2015 |website=[[TV by the Numbers]]}}</ref>
| ShortSummary    = Gordon takes Skye to Afterlife, a haven, where [[Lincoln Campbell]] explains to her that most people who are transformed are chosen and prepared for it, after which a guide is selected to help these people master their new abilities. Skye's guide is the founder of Afterlife, Jiaying, while Gordon will guide Raina, who still wants to die. When Gonzales asks Fitz and Simmons to help them open Fury's toolbox, Fitz refuses and decides to leave S.H.I.E.L.D., while Simmons agrees to help, though this is a ruse so that Fitz can take the toolbox with him. Coulson and Hunter steal a quinjet from Gonzales' agents with the help of Agent [[Mike Peterson (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Mike Peterson]], who has been hunting Hydra scientist Dr. [[List (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|List]] and found him experimenting on gifted people. With the appearance of Peterson, Gonzales fears how many super powered operatives Coulson has, but believes that he still deserves fair representation, asking May to serve on their S.H.I.E.L.D. board. Coulson realizes that, to deal with the new Hydra threat, he will have to turn to Grant Ward.
| LineColor       = 881E1E
}}
